+# 9. Due times
+
+Date: 2026-11-15
+Status: Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The help desk is starting to promise response times: 4 hours for an urgent ticket, 24 for high, 72 for normal and 168
+for low. Tickets need a due time, the hours must be changeable without a release, and the production data file already
+holds tickets. The change must also be reversible: if the release misbehaves, operators go back to 1.4.0 on the file the
+new release wrote.
+
+## Decision
+
+We will give every ticket a `due`: its creation time plus the hours of its priority at creation.
+
+- The hours are settings, `RESPONSE_HOURS_URGENT`, `_HIGH`, `_NORMAL` and `_LOW`, read at start.
+- The due time is stored on the ticket and set once. The store never recomputes it, so a later change of the hours or of
+  the ticket's priority does not move it. It is not an audit change: the audit log is as before.
+- `due` is a field of the ticket record in the data file (`src/persistence.js`). The format stays version 1 and no other
+  field changes meaning. Release 1.4.0 refuses any other version and ignores a ticket field it does not know, so it
+  starts on the new file and shows every ticket.
+- When the store opens a file with tickets that have no due time (a file from before this release, or one that 1.4.0
+  rewrote), it gives each its due time from its own creation time and the priority it has then, and saves the file at
+  once. This happens whether or not due times are on, so the file holds them before they are switched on.
+- `DUE_TIMES=on` switches the feature on: the API then shows `due` and answers `GET /tickets?overdue=true` (open and
+  in-progress tickets whose due time has passed). Otherwise the API answers exactly as before; `overdue` is then an
+  unknown parameter and ignored.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Rolling out is two steps: deploy with `DUE_TIMES` off (the file is filled), then switch it on. Rolling back needs no
+  data migration.
+- Release 1.4.0 does not keep `due` when it saves, so going back and forward again recomputes the due times of every
+  ticket from creation time and priority.
+- A new field of a ticket is added to the record functions in `src/persistence.js`, or it is lost at the next restart
+  (decision 8).
